:: day2_hub [nobr]
<!--
  PLACEHOLDER   pipeline test only, AND the current end of the
  public build's content (female route).
  Day 0 and Day 1 are both real, playable content as of v0.2, so
  the female route flows straight through them without any "end of
  build" interruption   the notice only fires here, once the player
  actually runs out of written content. Uses its own
  <<endOfContentNoticeFemale>> widget (widgets.tw), distinct from the
  futa route's <<endOfContentNoticeFuta>> at day1_hub_futa.tw, since
  the two routes are at different points and the messages diverged.
  Replace with real Day 2 ("Body") content and its own day2fInit
  flag block (mirroring day1f-init.tw) when written   at that point,
  move the <<endOfContentNoticeFemale>> call below down to wherever
  the new content's own final passage ends.
-->
<div class="day-transition">
  <h2><<print formatDayNumber($dayNumber)>>   Body</h2>
  <p>(Day 2 content not yet written. Days -2 through Day 1 are
  fully playable end to end on the female route   the Rite, the
  first day of recovery in the Moonspire Tower, and everything
  before it.)</p>
  <p><<print $mcName>>, <<print $mcTitle>>. Height <<print $mcHeight>>,
  bust <<print $mcBust>>. Stress: <<print $stress>> | Energy: <<print $energy>></p>
</div>

<<endOfContentNoticeFemale>>
